<b>The End of the World</b>

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.990
Who are these guys, anyway?!

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:23.550
{split}They sure know how to handle those GINNs!

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:29.540
The workers are to continue with the demolition!

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:31.760
If we stop, we'll be playing right into their hands!

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:43.150
You've gotta be kidding! Who the hell fights in this kind of area?!

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:46.950
Were you the ones who set the colony in motion?!

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:52.870
<b></b>

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:00.100
What the...

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:02.300
{split}Chaos, Gaia and Abyss?!

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:04.630
The machines stolen from Armory One!

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:10.110
It's them!

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:13.690
<i>We'll get those three today!</i>

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:15.640
Those machines are not our objective!

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:17.120
I know that!

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:19.100
But they're attacking us!

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:22.020
Unless we get rid of them, we won't get any work done, will we?!

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:29.320
Junius Seven's descent angle has increased by 1.5! Four percent acceleration!

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:34.020
The Joule Team is under attack by the Chaos, the Gaia and the Abyss!

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:37.090
They're unable to continue with the demolition work.

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:39.710
Captain! We should go after Bogey One!

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:46.630
Mr. Chairman, what is your assessment of Bogey One's current involvement?

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:51.260
Pirates? Or part of the Earth Forces?

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:54.060
That's a difficult question.

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:57.610
I would rather not get into a battle with the Earth Forces.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:01.940
There's no saying what it could trigger, after all.

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:18.790
But the situation has changed.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:19.460
Yes.

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:23.880
The situation is critical; if they declare themselves to be with the Earth Forces

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:29.970
or associated with them in some way, fighting them here would be meaningless.

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:46.020
On the contrary, they could be interpreting our actions as protecting those GINNs.

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:47.190
They couldn't be!

00:07:47.470 --> 00:07:48.590
It's entirely possible.

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:50.610
If those machines happened to be Daggers,

00:07:50.890 --> 00:07:53.780
you'd be suspicious of the Earth Forces and their participation, wouldn't you?

00:07:57.070 --> 00:07:59.290
Can we get in touch with Bogey One?

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:01.710
We could use the International Rescue Channel.

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:03.660
Then reach out to them.

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:08.710
Make it clear to them that we are making every effort to crush Junius Seven and stop it from falling to Earth.

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:23.730
Damn!

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:27.940
What?

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:34.660
Stop it!

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:50.210
Who is this guy?! He's strong!

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:18.530
This'll finish you, Red Suit!

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:20.790
Not so fast!

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:19.010
<i>I must inform you all of a very serious situation</i>.

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:25.570
<i>As rumored, Junius Seven has drifted out of its orbit</i>

00:10:25.570 --> 00:10:27.520
<i>and is currently approaching Earth</i>.

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:29.050
Birdy.

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:32.730
Birdy.

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:38.950
<i>The Orb government has formed an alliance with the governments of the world</i>

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:41.290
<i>and has discussed the best way to deal with the situation</i>.

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:42.760
<i>Unfortunately, given the lack of time</i>,

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:47.830
<i>we have yet to come up with an effective solution</i>.

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:50.750
Hey! Wait! Wait, Birdy!

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:54.210
How in the world can it fall this fast?!

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.340
We have no information about that at this time.

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:58.340
<i>Will it be possible to avoid impact?!</i>

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:02.230
<i>What is the estimated time of impact, and estimated point of impact?!</i>

00:11:02.230 --> 00:11:06.770
<i>Currently, the PLANTs and Earth Alliance Forces are working together to crush the object to pieces</i>.

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:10.240
<i>We must inform the citizens of this critical situation</i>,

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:13.650
<i>and have people make their way to the shelters immediately</i>.

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:15.370
<i>Is there enough time?!</i>

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:17.360
<i>What are the chances the demolition op will succeed?!</i>

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:21.030
<i>There isn't enough room in the shelters to accommodate the world's population!</i>

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:25.640
Hurry! It might still be too late even if we do manage to split it!

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:46.040
<i>It's secure!</i>

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:46.570
<i>Good!</i>

00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:12.890
Great! We did it!

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:27.120
Why, that's...

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:32.020
What's going on here?!

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:33.580
That thing just split in two!

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:38.670
But we're not done yet!

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:42.480
<i>We need to break it into smaller pieces</i>.

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:43.760
Athrun?!

00:13:44.020 --> 00:13:47.280
Bastard! What the hell are you doing here?!

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:49.220
<i>That's not important right now!</i>

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:51.030
We must continue with our mission!

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:52.450
<i>R-Right!</i>

00:13:52.740 --> 00:13:53.680
<i>I know that!</i>

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:57.310
You haven't changed, Yzak.

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:58.350
Neither have you!

00:13:59.110 --> 00:14:00.020
Oh, boy.

00:14:30.530 --> 00:14:31.760
Those guys!

00:14:37.840 --> 00:14:38.810
Yzak!

00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:39.940
Shut up!

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:45.030
I'm the one in command here! Stop giving orders!

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:47.690
You damn civilian!

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:51.660
Auel!

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:09.340
<i>So these are the abilities of the survivors of Jachin Due?</i>

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:20.060
<i>Shinn! What are you doing?! We're not finished with our mission yet!</i>

00:15:29.540 --> 00:15:31.400
Looks like they finally believe us.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:35.880
That may be true, or there could be another reason.

00:15:36.310 --> 00:15:37.330
Another reason?

00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:38.750
The altitude.

00:15:41.820 --> 00:15:45.170
If we continue to fall with Junius Seven,

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:49.070
the ship won't be able to escape Earth's gravity.

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:53.000
We must decide now what lives we cannot afford to lose.

00:15:53.940 --> 00:15:56.920
Who we can save, and who we cannot.

00:15:57.870 --> 00:15:58.640
Captain...

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:01.810
I'm sorry to have to bring this up under the circumstances,

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:05.060
but please make your way over to the Voltaire.

00:16:06.350 --> 00:16:08.990
The Minerva will now descend into the atmosphere for as long as possible

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:13.530
and continue to tear down the objective using our main cannon.

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:17.910
What?! C-Captain! You can't be...

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:27.250
I don't know how much more we can do, but it wouldn't be right if we didn't try everything we could.

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:29.200
But Talia...

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:32.540
I'm a woman with lots of luck.

00:16:32.790 --> 00:16:33.880
Please trust me.

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:40.470
All right. Thanks, Talia. I appreciate it.

00:16:40.840 --> 00:16:43.980
Thank you. Now, please hurry, Mr. Chairman.

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:45.930
Let's go, Miss.

00:16:46.490 --> 00:16:49.480
Tell the Voltaire that Chairman Durandal is on his way!

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:51.440
Send out a retreat signal to the mobile suits!

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.400
I'm staying here.

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:57.340
Athrun hasn't returned yet.

00:16:57.970 --> 00:17:02.870
If the Minerva will go to such lengths to protect the Earth, then I shall join you!

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:07.370
However, there are other duties where statespersons are required.

00:17:07.740 --> 00:17:11.630
If you insist, Miss Representative, I shall respect that.

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:17.640
We've reached critical altitude!

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:21.760
Will the Minerva continue to descend while firing its main cannon?

00:17:38.550 --> 00:17:43.730
<i>Attention all hands! Upon retrieving all mobile suits, this ship will continue attacking the objective with the main cannon</i>

00:17:43.730 --> 00:17:46.130
<i>while descending into Earth's atmosphere</i>.

00:17:46.550 --> 00:17:47.170
What?!

00:17:47.600 --> 00:17:51.170
All hands are expected to review their manuals and take appropriate action.

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:04.220
<i>What are you doing?!</i>

00:18:05.320 --> 00:18:08.690
Orders have been given for us to return! You should've received the notice!

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:12.110
Yeah, I know. You'd better hurry on back.

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:15.690
You'll end up being blasted away! Are you okay with that?!

00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:18.070
Even with a cannon like Minerva's!

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:20.870
There's a greater margin for error if you fire at a distance.

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:22.680
<i>So if we can at least get this one going</i>...

00:18:27.140 --> 00:18:30.170
Why would someone like you side with Orb?

00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:38.880
I won't let you do any more damage!

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:41.850
These guys are still here!

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:57.210
My daughter's tombstone must be dropped and burned for this world to change!

00:18:58.950 --> 00:18:59.930
Daughter?

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:01.450
What the...

00:19:03.100 --> 00:19:06.590
Why have you forgotten the sorrow of the lives mercilessly thrown away here?!

00:19:06.590 --> 00:19:11.040
Why do you live in a fabricated world, laughing with those who caused this?!

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:17.290
Tricked by the cowardly successors of Clyne...

00:19:17.780 --> 00:19:20.030
ZAFT has changed for the worse!

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:43.240
Why can't you realize

00:19:46.130 --> 00:19:52.080
that for us Coordinators, the path of Patrick Zala was the one and only correct path!

00:20:20.180 --> 00:20:21.110
Shinn!

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:44.750
Descent sequence, phase two!

00:20:46.400 --> 00:20:48.350
Where are the Impulse and that guy's ZAKU?!

00:20:48.780 --> 00:20:51.360
We don't know! I can't get their position!

00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:52.260
Athrun!

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:57.940
This time for sure, we'll let those Naturals have it!

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:40.440
Now, come over here, everybody. Please follow me.

00:21:40.740 --> 00:21:41.780
What is it?

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:42.930
Where are we going?

00:21:43.100 --> 00:21:45.270
Oh, I know! Shopping, right?!

00:21:45.270 --> 00:21:47.300
I still wanna play.

00:21:48.990 --> 00:21:49.800
Kira?

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:59.840
<b>tooku hanareteru hodo ni chikaku ni kanjiteru</b>

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:59.840
<b>The further we are apart, the nearer I feel you are</b>

00:21:59.840 --> 00:22:10.510
<b>samishisa mo tsuyosa eto kawatteku... kimi wo omottanara</b>

00:21:59.840 --> 00:22:10.510
<b>Even my loneliness turns into strength... when I think of you</b>

00:22:18.400 --> 00:22:25.820
<b>kotoba wo kasanete mo wakari aenai koto</b>

00:22:18.400 --> 00:22:25.820
I still did not realize

00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:32.620
<b>
mada shiranakatta ne</b>

00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:32.620
That there are things that can't be conveyed even with words

00:22:31.910 --> 00:22:40.250
<b>kimi dake wo dakishimetakute nakushita yume kimi wa</b>

00:22:31.910 --> 00:22:40.250
My lost dreams of wanting to hold you by my side,

00:22:39.580 --> 00:22:47.220
<b>
"akiramenaide" to itta</b>

00:22:39.580 --> 00:22:47.220
For them, you said, "Don't give up!"

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:54.060
<b>tooku hanareteru hodo ni chikaku ni kanjiteru</b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:54.060
The further we are apart, the nearer I feel you are

00:22:53.350 --> 00:23:02.190
<b>
samishisa mo tsuyosa eto kawatteku... kimi wo omottanara</b>

00:22:53.350 --> 00:23:02.190
Even my loneliness turns into strength... when I think of you

00:23:01.520 --> 00:23:08.900
<b>setsunaku mune wo sasu sore wa yume no kakera</b>

00:23:01.520 --> 00:23:08.900
The thing that pierces the gentle chest, that's a fragment of my dream

